# Review: SpacetimePlugin

Most of the spec is built. The `Scene` and `Model.Object` ECHO types, the select, move and extrude
tools, the toolbar, OBJ/GLB import, STL export and join/subtract all exist under `src/`. The
geometry engine is well tested: `boolean-ops.test.ts`, `extrusion.test.ts` and `obj-import.test.ts`
cover union, ordered difference, result position, extrusion, clamping and OBJ conversion. The UI
side has almost no tests: tools, actions, keyboard handling and the canvas are exercised only by
stories without play functions, so most interaction requirements are `untested` and four of the
five acceptance scenarios have no automation.

Three findings matter most:

- **Remote edits do not re-render.** The canvas syncs meshes from ECHO only when `objectCount`
  changes, so a peer moving or recolouring an object is not shown until an object is added or
  removed (FR-1.4).
- **There is no `ManifoldService`.** Code calls `getManifold()` and the Manifold API directly; the
  `InvalidGeometry` and `WasmNotReady` errors do not exist.
- **Selection shape differs.** The code has three variants (`object`, `multi-object`, `face`), not
  `ObjectSelection { objects, primary }`, and the move tool collapses a multi-selection to one object
  on pointer-up.

